    "result_text": "All tests pass. The repository contains a single test class (`AcceptanceTest`); the other two files are an abstract base and a helper. `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures/errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment (`<LAST3>-<NNNN>`) with minimal structural impact \u2014 reusing the owner list already fetched in `addOwner` rather than adding a new query, service method, or injected collaborator.\n\nChanges (5 files, each edit small and self-contained):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `readOnly` `customerCode` string to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field and MapStruct auto-maps it by name (no mapper change needed).\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `customer_code` column with a plain getter/setter.\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, reused the existing `findAllOwners()` result for both the telephone check and the sequence count, then set:\n   ```java\n   last.substring(0, Math.min(3, last.length())).toUpperCase() + String.format(\"-%04d\", existingOwners.size() + 1)\n   ```\n   `Math.min` guards short last names without adding a branch (CC unchanged).\n4. **`db/hsqldb/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` column (test DB uses `ddl-auto=none`, so the DDL is required).\n5. **`db/hsqldb/data.sql`** \u2014 appended a trailing `NULL` to the 10 positional seed inserts to match the new column.\n\nThe code is `SMI-0007`-style: first three letters of `lastName` upper-cased, plus a global zero-padded sequence equal to `(current owner count) + 1`, satisfying the \"consecutive create \u2192 +1\" assertion in the test.",
